This project is a Rust rewrite inspired by illuminate
(https://github.com/johnz4021/illuminate), and carries parts of it over.
Those parts remain under illuminate's MIT license, reproduced below.

Carried over from illuminate (read at commit 7a88df6, 2026-11-26):

- crates/nonio-core/src/{format,check,edit,base,repo,screens,code}.rs:
  ported from packages/core/src/*.ts (map format, checker, readers).
- crates/nonio-facts/src/{contract,settle,fetches}.rs: ported from
  packages/facts/src/contracts/facts.ts, settleCalls in
  packages/facts/src/facts/extract.ts, and packages/facts/src/journeys/fetches.ts.
- crates/nonio-core/tests/*.rs: ported from packages/core/test/*.test.ts.
- crates/nonio-core/tests/fixtures/care-app, care-app.map.json and
  care-app.journey.json: copied from packages/core/test/fixtures.
- crates/nonio-core/tests/fixtures/recorded-facts.json: produced by
  illuminate's own extractor (see tools/record-facts).
- crates/nonio-scan/src/{extract,walk,record,resolve,entries,adapters,tables,
  routes,fallback,hash}.rs: ported from packages/facts/src/facts/*.ts and
  packages/facts/src/imports.ts (TS/JS extraction).
- crates/nonio-scan/tests/{extract,imports,resolve,tables}.rs: ported from
  packages/facts/test/*.test.ts.
- crates/nonio-scan/tests/fixtures/alias-repo: copied from
  packages/facts/test/fixtures.
- tools/compare-facts/dump.ts: calls illuminate's createFactsIndex.
- crates/nonio-server/src/{bridge,host,request,store}.rs: ported from
  packages/server/src/{bridge,host,store}.ts and requestText/partsOf in
  packages/server/src/channel.ts (host messages and request wording).
- crates/nonio-server/tests/{bridge,request}.rs: ported from
  packages/server/test/channel.test.ts.
- crates/nonio-server/src/{prompts,hints,changes,maker,scan}.rs: ported from
  packages/server/src/{prompts,hints,changes,maker}.ts, scanRepoFacts in
  packages/facts/src/scan.ts and diffSymbols in packages/facts/src/facts/diff.ts
  (the prompt text is illuminate's).
- crates/nonio-server/schemas/*.schema.json: illuminate's output schemas,
  written by packages/server/src/schemas.ts (see tools/record-prompts).
- crates/nonio-server/tests/fixtures/prompts: illuminate's prompts and head
  start on fixed inputs (see tools/record-prompts).
- crates/nonio-server/tests/{maker,hints,changes}.rs: ported from
  packages/server/test/{workflows,proposals,journeys,hints,changes}.test.ts.
- crates/nonio-server/src/{explainer,fixes,reply,ids}.rs: ported from
  packages/server/src/{explainer,fixes,reply}.ts.
- crates/nonio-server/tests/{explainer,fixes,reply}.rs: ported from
  packages/server/test/{workflows,proposals,reply,changes}.test.ts.
- crates/nonio-server/src/{server,step}.rs: ported from
  packages/server/src/{server,step,git}.ts.
- crates/nonio-server/src/screens.rs: ported from
  packages/server/src/screens.ts (the in-page reader script is illuminate's).
- crates/nonio-server/tests/{server,offers,selection,stop}.rs: ported from
  packages/server/test/{server,offers,selection,stop}.test.ts.
- crates/nonio-server/tests/screens.rs: ported from
  packages/server/test/screens.test.ts.
- crates/nonio-server/src/{channel,browser}.rs: ported from
  packages/server/src/{channel,browser}.ts (the MCP channel and its tools,
  renamed nonio_*).
- crates/nonio-server/tests/channel.rs: ported from
  packages/server/test/channel.test.ts.
- viewer/: packages/viewer (the web viewer, React Flow + ELK), with its tests,
  renamed for nonio (token header, storage keys, wording); viewer/src/model.d.ts
  was generated from packages/core and packages/server types. The logo is new.
- crates/nonio-cli/src/main.rs: after packages/server/src/cli.ts and runChannel
  in packages/server/src/channel.ts.
- crates/nonio-server/examples/preview.rs: after packages/server/scripts/preview.ts.
- tools/record-prompts/*.ts: call illuminate's prompt and schema modules.

The Vue template lowering in crates/nonio-scan/src/vue.rs is ported from
vue_oxlint_jsx 0.15.0 (vue-oxlint-toolkit,
https://github.com/liangmiQwQ/vue-oxlint-toolkit), src/parser/{parse,script,
elements/*}.rs: SFC blocks, template elements, directives, v-for, v-slot and
v-if lowered to JSX in one oxc Program. That part remains under
vue-oxlint-toolkit's MIT license, reproduced at the end of this file.

